  <data name="DitherHelp.AdaptiveHybrid"><value>In the current RIP, this compatibility option uses Ordered for variable-drop printing. Choose Ordered directly: this option currently provides no separate adaptive quality benefit.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.BlueNoiseFM"><value>Uses a blue-noise threshold mask to reduce the regular appearance of the dot pattern. Suitable for photos and smooth sky gradients; fine grain or residual mask texture may remain visible.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.CoupledED"><value>Coordinates dot placement within C/M and LC/LM pairs using error diffusion and tone-dependent threshold noise. Suitable for printers with both pairs; dot overlap and the balance between paired inks can change. Check a test print using your tone curves.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.CoupledEDCM"><value>Coordinates dot placement within the C/M pair; light inks and other channels remain independent. Suitable for four-colour printers or when LC/LM coupling is unwanted; it changes C/M overlap and texture without coupling the light-ink pair.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.EntropyZhouFang"><value>Adjusts Zhou-Fang threshold modulation using tone and local image structure. Suitable for detailed photos with smooth areas; it requires additional computation and can change the rendering of fine texture.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.Fast"><value>Uses a small ordered threshold matrix with variable drop sizes. Suitable for simple graphics and test prints; gradients may show a more visible repeating pattern, and the name does not guarantee faster processing.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.Ordered"><value>Places ink drops of different sizes using a fixed threshold matrix. Suitable for test charts and graphics; smooth tonal gradients may show a repeating raster pattern.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.Ostromoukhov"><value>Distributes quantization error to neighbouring pixels with tone-dependent weights. Suitable for detailed photos and tonal transitions; some tones may show directional dot chains.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.VeryFast"><value>Uses only the largest available drop at each selected dot position. Suitable for rough test prints; grain is coarser and highlight gradation can suffer. Faster processing is not guaranteed.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.X2Y1"><value>Uses error diffusion with alternating row direction, four-neighbour weights and tone-dependent noise modulation. Suitable for skies, sunsets and broad tonal gradients; fine grain or directional texture may remain visible.</value></data>
  <data name="DitherHelp.ZhouFang"><value>Adds tone-dependent quantization threshold modulation to error diffusion to reduce regular dot structures in midtones. Suitable for gradients that show patterns with Ostromoukhov; grain may become more noticeable.</value></data>
